  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>A small sandy cove with clear, shaded water, Graniers beach lies at the foot of the south slope of Saint-Tropez's Citadel, past the marine cemetery. It is only 94 metres long and bounded by rocks to the east and west; according to the tourist office, it has kept a wild, natural feel. A marine path runs nearby.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>As on all the town's beaches, municipal order no. 1828/2026 of 6 July 2026 (published on 21 July 2026 on saint-tropez.fr) allows dogs on the town's beaches every day, from 6am to 9.30am and 6.30pm to 10pm, from Thursday 16 July to Tuesday 15 September 2026; outside those hours they are not allowed. Dogs must stay under the constant responsibility of their owner or keeper and be kept on a leash when approaching other users and whenever circumstances require. Owners must pick up droppings immediately, preserve public peace, avoid any damage to natural areas and respect wildlife and plants.</p>
      <p>The order does not apply to guide or assistance dogs, to rescue, police or security dogs on duty, or to walkers with dogs on a leash on the coastal path. Offences may be penalised under the laws and regulations in force. The text only covers summer 2026: for the rest of the year, no published rule was found.</p>
      <p>This beach's listing on the tourist office's site (sainttropeztourisme.com) says "dogs are not allowed", with no mention of hours. The two official sources therefore disagree; the municipal order is the most recent and most precise text, but the signage on site on the day of your visit remains the reference.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the beach is small (94 m); in summer, the allowed windows for your dog are 6am-9.30am and 6.30pm-10pm.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The little <a href="/en/fiche-plages-centre-ville-saint-tropez">Ponche and Fontanette beaches</a> lie at the foot of the old village; <a href="/en/fiche-plage-canebiers-saint-tropez">Canebiers beach</a> is further east.</p>
